insert into public.projects (slug, number, name, eyebrow, short, description, tags, github, status, accent, problem, solution, architecture, decisions, reliability, published, sort_order)
values
('legacylens','01','LegacyLens','Agentic software modernization','Analyze legacy repositories, plan migrations, transform code, and validate behavior with automated quality gates.','An agentic modernization platform that treats migration as an engineering workflow rather than a one-shot code translation. It combines repository intelligence, planning, transformation, dependency awareness, post-migration validation, provenance, and release gating.','["Agentic AI","Code Intelligence","Agno","FastAPI","Docker"]','https://github.com/AsaifAli/AI-Code-Modernization-Platform','Deployed','cyan','Legacy migration is difficult to trust when translation, dependency changes, validation, and release readiness are handled as disconnected steps.','A staged multi-agent workflow performs discovery, planning, conversion, semantic validation, repair, and release gating while retaining evidence and migration state.','["Upload / source workspace","Repository scanner + code intelligence","Agentic planning + transformation","Knowledge / dependency analysis","Post-migration validation + repair","Release gate + reports"]','["Keep deterministic validation outside the LLM","Make migration state observable and resumable","Treat repair as a re-validation loop","Separate provider/model configuration from workflow logic"]','["Quality gates","Semantic verification","Security/provenance checks","CI regression tests","Persisted migration status"]',true,1),
('evidenceflow','02','EvidenceFlow','Verified RAG & research','Hybrid retrieval, reranking, web research, evidence verification, and fail-closed answer generation.','A LangGraph-based RAG system designed around evidence rather than raw model confidence. It routes between knowledge-base retrieval and web research, uses hybrid retrieval with reciprocal-rank fusion and reranking, and verifies answer claims against collected evidence.','["LangGraph","Qdrant","BM25","RRF","Tavily"]','https://github.com/AsaifAli/LangGraph-RAG','Deployed','violet','RAG systems can retrieve plausible text while still producing unsupported claims or overconfident answers.','The pipeline separates retrieval, evidence synthesis, citation verification, and answer policy so unsupported responses can fail closed instead of being presented as fact.','["Query understanding + routing","Dense + lexical retrieval","RRF fusion + cross-encoder reranking","Evidence synthesis","Citation / claim verification","Final guarded response"]','["Preserve evidence IDs through the graph","Keep tool execution provider-agnostic","Use deterministic citation checks","Separate document summaries from chunk analysis"]','["Evidence-grounded synthesis","Citation verification","Fail-closed behavior","Hybrid retrieval","Regression diagnostics"]',true,2),
('quotesense','03','QuoteSense','Procurement intelligence','Turn messy quotations into validated, comparable procurement intelligence with deterministic scoring and review.','A quotation-analysis workflow that deliberately separates probabilistic document extraction from deterministic business logic. LLM output is normalized into typed structures before scoring, risk checks, anomaly detection, and comparative reporting.','["Document AI","Pydantic","FastAPI","Procurement"]','https://github.com/AsaifAli/quotation-analyzer','Deployed','amber','Procurement documents contain inconsistent structure, missing values, and commercial edge cases that are risky to evaluate with free-form LLM reasoning alone.','Extract structured fields, validate with schemas, then apply deterministic calculations and business rules before generating the final interpretation.','["Document ingestion","LLM extraction","Pydantic validation","Deterministic calculations","Comparison + anomaly analysis","Human-readable result"]','["Keep arithmetic deterministic","Validate before scoring","Preserve raw extraction for auditability","Make provider choice independent of business rules"]','["Typed schemas","Deterministic scoring","Anomaly detection","Validation failures surfaced explicitly"]',true,3),
('flowpilot','04','FlowPilot','Agentic automation','Asynchronous AI workflows with approvals, evidence, persistence, and observability.','A production-minded automation command center where AI workflows run as durable jobs instead of fragile synchronous prompts. Human approval, execution state, validation, and observability are first-class parts of the design.','["LangGraph","FastAPI","Redis/RQ","PostgreSQL","Observability"]','https://github.com/AsaifAli/AI-Automation-Command-Center','Deployed','blue','LLM automation becomes difficult to operate when long-running work, retries, approvals, and state are hidden inside a request-response cycle.','Separate orchestration from execution, persist workflow state, and expose progress and approval boundaries explicitly.','["API command center","Workflow definition","Queue + worker execution","Persistence + state transitions","Approval / validation","Result + observability"]','["Use async jobs for long-running AI work","Persist state outside process memory","Keep human approval explicit","Treat provider failures as recoverable states"]','["Retryable workers","Persisted state","Approval gates","Request correlation","Health/readiness checks"]',true,4),
('webqa-intelligence','05','WebQA Intelligence','AI-assisted web QA','Discover dynamic web interactions, score QA risk, generate evidence-grounded tests, and compare regressions.','A browser-intelligence system built around Playwright that turns dynamic sites into testable evidence. It combines DOM analysis, interaction discovery, browser health signals, QA scoring, evidence-grounded test generation, and regression comparison.','["Playwright","Browser Automation","QA","Agents"]','https://github.com/AsaifAli/Web-Crawler-Agent','Deployed','green','Static crawlers miss dynamic interactions, delayed content, and real user-flow risk.','Use a real browser to observe behavior, collect evidence, identify meaningful interactions, and feed that evidence into QA analysis and test generation.','["Browser session","DOM + interaction discovery","Browser health signals","Risk scoring","Evidence-grounded test generation","Regression comparison"]','["Use Playwright for runtime truth","Capture evidence before generating tests","Separate crawler telemetry from LLM reasoning","Treat browser failures as first-class signals"]','["Browser health telemetry","Evidence-backed tests","Regression comparison","Bounded crawl behavior"]',true,5)
